Fix Hyprland compositor crash when the session is locked while a grabbing
xdg_popup (owned by a layer surface, e.g. a bar dropdown/menu) is open.

Root cause: CSessionLockProtocol::onLock emits `newLock` -- which runs the
entire session-lock setup, including CSeatManager::setGrab(nullptr) -- BEFORE
setting m_locked = true, so the popup grab is torn down while isSessionLocked()
is still false and the lock-time guards in the focus/grab paths are bypassed.
Ending the grab dismisses the popup (CSeatGrab end -> done() -> dismissed ->
CPopup::onUnmap) mid-transition. Several CPopup / CSeatManager sites guard an
OUTER weak pointer with operator bool / valid() (which stays true while the
object is destroying()) then dereference an INNER pointer with no check, so the
inner wl_surface (or owner) being null/destroying during the teardown race
faults. Hardened to the .expired()+inner-check convention already used by
CPopup::coordsRelativeToParent() and CPopup::t1ParentCoords().

Applies to Hyprland v0.56.0 through v0.56.2 (Popup.cpp and SeatManager.cpp are
byte-identical across those tags). Not fixed upstream as of main@36b2e0c.
See docs/hyprland-popup-lock-crash for the full analysis and upstream PR text.
